    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.operators\n\n### Question\n\nReally like the functions provided in mini.operators. Could someone give an example how to remap default `gx` (open link/file) and `gr` (go to reference) to other key, like `<leader>gx` `<leader>gr` ? thanks! ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.operators</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Really like the functions provided in mini.operators. Could someone give an example how to remap default <code class=\"notranslate\">gx</code> (open link/file) and <code class=\"notranslate\">gr</code> (go to reference) to other key, like <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;leader&gt;gx</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;leader&gt;gr</code> ? thanks!</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.operators\nQuestion\nReally like the functions provided in mini.operators. Could someone give an example how to remap default gx (open link/file) and gr (go to reference) to other key, like <leader>gx <leader>gr ? thanks!",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
