    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-01-05T09:48:10Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Here is [how I remap built-in `gx`](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/935ca1849601987275805ec45fe8b0c6db41e60a/plugin/20_mini.lua#L219-L226).\r\n\r\nThe `gr` mapping for \"go to reference\" may vary for you. Chances are, you mean map to `vim.lsp.buf.references()` which can be done as a usual mapping. I prefer something like this: `vim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>gr', '<Cmd>lua vim.lsp.buf.references()<CR>', { desc = 'References' })`.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Here is <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/935ca1849601987275805ec45fe8b0c6db41e60a/plugin/20_mini.lua#L219-L226\">how I remap built-in <code class=\"notranslate\">gx</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">gr</code> mapping for \"go to reference\" may vary for you. Chances are, you mean map to <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.lsp.buf.references()</code> which can be done as a usual mapping. I prefer something like this: <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;gr', '&lt;Cmd&gt;lua vim.lsp.buf.references()&lt;CR&gt;', { desc = 'References' })</code>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Here is how I remap built-in gx.\nThe gr mapping for \"go to reference\" may vary for you. Chances are, you mean map to vim.lsp.buf.references() which can be done as a usual mapping. I prefer something like this: vim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>gr', '<Cmd>lua vim.lsp.buf.references()<CR>', { desc = 'References' }).",
